1. Purpose

Code to run analytical metrics in the ETK using a general structure. Thought to be used with BBH metric.

2. Instructions.

To run a superposed binary black hole run follow roughlt these steps:
	
	1) Generate trajectories for the BBHs. For this you need to generate an hdf5 file using the program CBWave inside this repo.
	   Once you compile inside CBWave/src/ (make all) you can run it using driver_PN_run.py (python driver_PN_run.py). You can
	   open this .py file to change initial data and other properties.

	2) Once you have the trajectories, you might run it in the ETK using the following in your parfile:

             #=======================
             # Analytical Spacetime
             # ======================
             
             ActiveThorns = "AnalyticalSpacetime"
             AnalyticalSpacetime::analytical_metric_type = "SuperposedBBH" 
             AnalyticalSpacetime::traj_read_table = "yes"
             
             # Replace this with your trajectory table
             AnalyticalSpacetime::traj_table_name ="/home/d/dsiegel/lcombi/repository/analyticalbbh/CBwaves/src/CircularOrbit_a0_m05_sep10.h5"
             # This will adjust the mass. Useful for very near merger where the (fake) mass grows (sperations <5M).
             AnalyticalSpacetime::AST_adjust_mass1 = 1.0
             AnalyticalSpacetime::AST_adjust_mass2 = 1.0
             
             # This sets a scalar with the position of the black hole similar to TwoPuncture tracker
             AnalyticalSpacetime::set_positions = "yes"
             AnalyticalSpacetime::surf_storage_BH1 = 0
             AnalyticalSpacetime::surf_storage_BH2 = 1
             
             ADMBase::initial_lapse = "analytical_spacetime"
             ADMBase::initial_shift = "analytical_spacetime"
             ADMBase::initial_data = "analytical_spacetime"
             ADMBase::evolution_method = "analytical_spacetime"
             ADMBase::metric_type = "physical"
             
             # The following is to evolve the metric only once every 128 iterations.
             # Change standard options if evolving every timestep.
             
             AnalyticalSpacetime::evolve_metric_every = 128
             ADMBase::lapse_prolongation_type = "none"
             ADMBase::shift_prolongation_type = "none"
             ADMBase::metric_prolongation_type = "none"
             
             ADMBase::metric_timelevels = 3
             ADMBase::lapse_timelevels = 3
             ADMBase::shift_timelevels = 3

             
